# Snoglode: 4-Version Comparison & Recommendation

## Overview

The four versions share the same core algorithm ([solver.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/solver.py), [branching.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/components/branching.py), [node.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/components/node.py), [parameters.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/components/parameters.py), [compute.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/utils/compute.py), [ef.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/utils/ef.py) are **byte-identical** across all four). The differences are concentrated in **3 files** plus the example runner:

| File | EFfixed | ori-record3 | ori-record3-log | ori-record3v5 |
|------|---------|-------------|-----------------|---------------|
| [snoglode/solver.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/solver.py) | ✅ same | baseline | ✅ same | ✅ same |
| [snoglode/bounders/lower_bounders.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/bounders/lower_bounders.py) | ✅ same | baseline | ✅ same | ⚠️ **modified** |
| [snoglode/bounders/upper_bounders.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/bounders/upper_bounders.py) | ✅ same | baseline | 🔧 logging only | ⚠️ **modified** |
| [snoglode/components/subproblems.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/components/subproblems.py) | ✅ same | baseline | ✅ same | ⚠️ **modified** |
| [snoglode/components/tree.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/components/tree.py) | ✅ same | baseline | 🔧 logging only | ✅ same |
| `examples/.../stochastic_pid.py` | ✅ same | baseline | 🔧 logging added | ⚠️ **modified** |
| Config: `num_scenarios` | 5 | 5 | 5 | **50** |
| Config: `rel_tolerance` | 1e-5 | 1e-5 | 1e-5 | **1e-6** |

---

## Version-by-Version Breakdown

### 1. `snoglode-main-2-ori-record3` — The Baseline

This is the **reference version**. All other versions derive from it.

Key characteristics:
- Timeout handling in [stochastic_pid.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/examples/stochastic_pid/stochastic_pid.py): uses Gurobi's dual bound (`results.problem.lower_bound`) directly when `maxTimeLimit` is hit; raises `RuntimeError` on any other unexpected termination condition
- In [lower_bounders.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/bounders/lower_bounders.py): only accepts `TerminationCondition.optimal` + `SolverStatus.ok`; raises `RuntimeError` otherwise
- In [upper_bounders.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/bounders/upper_bounders.py): uses a simple `else: return False, None` for non-optimal UB subproblems
- In [subproblems.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/snoglode/components/subproblems.py): simple `assert lb <= ub` with a hard `assert (delta <= 1e-8)` for bounds inversion repair

---

### 2. `snoglode-main-2-EFfixed` — Identical to Baseline

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **EFfixed is byte-identical to ori-record3 in every [.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/diff_versions.py) file.** Despite the name suggesting an "EF fix", no code differences exist. This version can be safely discarded as a duplicate.

---

### 3. `snoglode-main-2-ori-record3-log` — Baseline + Debug Logging

Changes are **purely additive logging** — no algorithmic behavior changes:

#### [tree.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-ori-record3-log/snoglode/components/tree.py)
- Adds `root.depth = 0` on root node initialization
- Propagates `depth` attribute to child nodes after branching

#### [upper_bounders.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-ori-record3-log/snoglode/bounders/upper_bounders.py)
- Stores `_debug_last_solver_status` and `_debug_last_tc` after EF solve for external logging

#### [stochastic_pid.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-ori-record3-log/examples/stochastic_pid/stochastic_pid.py)
- **Major addition**: ~100 lines of monkey-patched debug logging infrastructure:
  - `debug_reachtimelimit.txt` — records timed-out subproblems
  - `debug_log/debug_ef_solver.txt` — EF solver status per iteration
  - `debug_log/debug_dual.txt` — per-scenario dual bound details
  - `debug_log/debug_iter_info.txt` — per-iteration summary (LB, UB, gap, etc.)
- Wraps `dispatch_node_selection`, `solve_a_subproblem`, `dispatch_updates`, and `solve_ef` with logging hooks

> [!NOTE]
> These logging changes do **not** alter any algorithm behavior. The debug hooks only read solver state — they never modify decisions, bounds, or solutions.

---

### 4. `snoglode-main-2-ori-record3v5` — Baseline + Robustness Improvements

This version contains **significant algorithmic changes** for robustness:

#### [lower_bounders.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-ori-record3v5/snoglode/bounders/lower_bounders.py)
```diff
 # Acceptance condition broadened:
-if results.solver.termination_condition == TerminationCondition.optimal and \
-    results.solver.status == SolverStatus.ok:
+if (results.solver.termination_condition == TerminationCondition.optimal or \
+    results.solver.termination_condition == TerminationCondition.maxIterations) and \
+   (results.solver.status == SolverStatus.ok or results.solver.status == SolverStatus.warning):
```
- Adds `safely_get_lower_bound()` helper + `LB_FLOOR = -1e10` constant
- Replaces `RuntimeError` with robust fallback: tries solver's dual bound → successor objective → conservative `LB_FLOOR`
- Loads incumbent solution even on non-optimal termination (for warm-start)

#### [upper_bounders.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-ori-record3v5/snoglode/bounders/upper_bounders.py)
```diff
-else:
-    return False, None
+elif results.solver.termination_condition == TerminationCondition.infeasible:
+    return False, None
+else:
+    # Try to recover incumbent; if none, return inf (valid weak UB)
+    try:
+        subproblem_model.solutions.load_from(results)
+        obj = pyo.value(get_active_objective(subproblem_model))
+        if obj is not None: return True, obj
+    except: pass
+    return True, float('inf')
```
- Only returns [(False, None)](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/diff_versions.py#7-21) for truly infeasible; otherwise tries to recover an incumbent or returns `+inf` as a weak but valid UB

#### [subproblems.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-ori-record3v5/snoglode/components/subproblems.py)
- **Bounds validation overhaul**: Replaces `assert lb <= ub` with detailed NaN/inf checks, tiny inversion repair (midpoint), and `InconsistentBoundsError` for large inversions
- **Bounds tightening**: Adds safety checks after FBBT/OBBT with repair or `return False` for infeasible nodes
- **Feasibility check**: Uses `continue` instead of `return True` for `None` bounds; adds `math.isfinite()` check
- Adds two new methods: `unrelax_all_integers()` and `save_results_to_dict()`

#### [stochastic_pid.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-ori-record3v5/examples/stochastic_pid/stochastic_pid.py)
- **Timeout handling**: On `maxTimeLimit`, runs IPOPT as fallback for primal side-effects (instead of just using Gurobi's dual bound)
- **Catch-all termination**: Replaces `else: raise RuntimeError` with a 3-priority LB recovery strategy (solver dual bound → successor objective → LB_FLOOR/`-inf`)
- Removes `ApplicationError` import and `math` import (moved into library)
- Config: **`num_scenarios = 50`** (vs 5), **`rel_tolerance = 1e-6`** (vs 1e-5)

---

## Summary of Differences

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["ori-record3<br/>(Baseline)"] -->|identical| B["EFfixed"]
    A -->|+ debug logging<br/>no algo change| C["ori-record3-log"]
    A -->|+ robustness<br/>+ bounds validation<br/>+ error recovery| D["ori-record3v5"]
```

| Category | ori-record3 / EFfixed | ori-record3-log | ori-record3v5 |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Non-optimal termination** | `RuntimeError` (crash) | `RuntimeError` (crash) | Graceful recovery with fallback LB |
| **Bounds inversion** | `assert delta <= 1e-8` (crash) | Same as baseline | Midpoint repair or `InconsistentBoundsError` |
| **UB for non-infeasible timeout** | Returns [(False, None)](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/diff_versions.py#7-21) | Same as baseline | Tries incumbent, else returns `+inf` |
| **NaN/inf bounds check** | None | None | Explicit validation |
| **Debug logging** | None | ✅ Extensive | None |
| **IPOPT fallback on timeout** | No | No | ✅ Yes |
| **num_scenarios** | 5 | 5 | 50 |
| **rel_tolerance** | 1e-5 | 1e-5 | 1e-6 |

---

## Recommendation

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **For production/research runs, use `snoglode-main-2-ori-record3v5`** — it is the most robust version:
> - Won't crash on solver timeouts or unexpected termination conditions
> - Has proper bounds validation that prevents silent numerical corruption
> - Gracefully degrades with conservative fallback bounds instead of `RuntimeError`

> [!TIP]
> **However, note two config differences** in [stochastic_pid.py](file:///c:/Users/Administrator/OneDrive/Desktop/workspace2026/211%20choose%20version/snoglode-main-2-EFfixed/examples/stochastic_pid/stochastic_pid.py) that you may want to adjust:
> 1. `num_scenarios = 50` (vs 5 in others) — change this to match your intended experiment
> 2. `rel_tolerance = 1e-6` (vs 1e-5) — tighter tolerance means slower convergence; choose based on your accuracy needs

> [!NOTE]
> If you also need debug logging, the cleanest approach is to **merge the logging additions from ori-record3-log into ori-record3v5**. The logging changes are non-algorithmic and fully compatible — they only add read-only hooks around existing solver methods.
